---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Compare two OpenAPI documents and classify every difference as breaking, non-breaking or unknown; exits 1 on a breaking difference

Usage: rustman contract diff [OPTIONS] <OLD> [NEW]

Arguments:
  <OLD>
          The old document (a file or an http(s) URL); with --base, the document's path, read at the ref and from the working tree

  [NEW]
          The new document (a file or an http(s) URL)

Options:
      --base <REF>
          Read the old document (and the files its $refs name) from this git ref, as in origin/main

      --fail-on-unknown
          Exit 1 on unknown differences too

      --fail-on <CLASSIFICATION>
          The least severe classification that exits 1: breaking (default), unknown, or non-breaking for any difference (frozen APIs)
          
          [default: breaking]
          [possible values: breaking, unknown, non-breaking]

      --allowlist <FILE>
          The allowlist of accepted differences (default: contracts/allowlist.yaml in the workspace, or the current folder)

      --report <FORMAT[=PATH]>
          Also write the report as json, junit, markdown, html or sarif, to a file or stdout, as in markdown=out/contract.md (repeatable)

      --env <NAME>
          Environment whose secret values are redacted from the output (default: RUSTMAN_ENV, then default_environment)

      --workspace <DIR>
          Workspace directory (default: search from the current directory upwards; a diff needs none)

      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help
